    <ImplementationPlan>
      <T-001>
        <Title>kafedra-flow-intake: map the copied-address administrator journey and all recoverable states</Title>
        <DependsOn></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The flow covers idle, checking, connected, access code required, classified error, empty source, preview, import and repeated import.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Local people and work remain usable through every Docomator failure.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run docs:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-001>
      <T-002>
        <Title>kafedra-design: reduce the connection form to one stable address control</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-001 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The design artifact reduces the connection form to one address and one optional access code without changing the surrounding department structure geometry.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Desktop and mobile retain a clear order of address, connect, source, preview and import.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Endpoint, code and import action are never-learn; space and group are domain-derived or explicit current choices.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-002>
      <T-003>
        <Title>kafedra-motion: record the intentional no-motion behavior</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-002 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>No animation is introduced for connection, error, source or import states.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>With prefers-reduced-motion the same immediate state changes, focus and controls remain available.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-003>
      <T-004>
        <Title>kafedra-data: normalize endpoint input and preserve stored integration data</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-003 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>One parser accepts supported copied URLs and bare endpoints, strips only known Docomator paths and rejects credentials, query, fragment and unsupported schemes.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Legacy scheme, host and port rows remain the persisted representation and are exposed as one canonical url without migration.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The actual Docomator status ok readiness contract and legacy ready value are both supported.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Classified connection errors and idempotent people import remain deterministic and isolated from local records.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/docomator-integration.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-004>
      <T-005>
        <Title>kafedra-feature: implement the complete backend-to-UI Docomator path</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-004 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The administrator pastes one address, connects, selects the source and imports people without editing protocol or port separately.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The canonical endpoint is visible, the access code is not persisted, and failure never hides or disables local department data.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>One-space auto-selection, group refresh, field mapping, preview and repeated idempotent import work on desktop and mobile.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npx playwright test tests/browser/docomator-integration.spec.mjs tests/browser/docomator-fields.spec.mjs</Command><Command>npm run smoke</Command></Verification>
      </T-005>
      <T-006>
        <Title>kafedra-release: simplify secure archive staging and prove the active UI changed</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-005 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The source archive stays untouched in any readable user directory while extraction occurs in a private root staging directory without archived owners or permissions.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Installed release code remains root-owned; service data and configuration ownership contracts remain unchanged.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Static application responses cannot retain the previous non-fingerprinted UI after upgrade.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Post-update verification compares the selected bundle required UI files with active current before commit and rollback remains automatic on mismatch.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Operator docs explain root privilege boundaries and provide restart, status and log commands.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/deploy-install-contract.test.mjs tests/deployment-flow.test.mjs tests/static-cache.test.mjs</Command><Command>bash -n scripts/offline/install-from-archive.sh deploy/install.sh deploy/install-core.sh</Command></Verification>
      </T-006>
      <T-007>
        <Title>kafedra-design-audit: independently audit the implemented desktop and mobile path</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-006 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The audit checks hierarchy, focus, labels, target size, responsive layout, secrets, errors, empty states, partial success and no-motion behavior against the approved design.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Any blocking mismatch is fixed before the tests stage.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command><Command>npx playwright test tests/browser/docomator-integration.spec.mjs tests/browser/docomator-fields.spec.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-007>
      <T-008>
        <Title>kafedra-tests: run integration, deployment and regression gates</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-007 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Unit, integration, browser, upgrade, backup, restore, rollback and project regressions pass without weakening mandatory gates.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Desktop, mobile, accessibility, prefers-reduced-motion, error recovery, idempotency and local-directory independence are covered.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run check</Command><Command>npm run docs:check</Command><Command>npm test</Command><Command>npm run smoke</Command></Verification>
